1 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.dbgi.org/team/ruch-nicolas/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Patricia Malcolm</title><link>https://www.dbgi.org/team/malcolm-patricia/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.dbgi.org/team/malcolm-patricia/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Pierre-Marie Allard</title><link>https://www.dbgi.org/team/allard-pierre-marie/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.dbgi.org/team/allard-pierre-marie/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Pierre-Marie Allard launched the 
 &lt;a href="https://www.unifr.ch/bio/en/groups/allard/"&gt;COMMONS Lab&lt;/a&gt;
 at the Department of Biology of the University of Fribourg in 2021. He is also head of the Metabolomics Platform of the Department. His research interests focus on natural products, from their discovery to their structural elucidation, from the study of their uses by humans across the world to the understanding of their roles in the biosphere. The 
 &lt;a href="https://www.unifr.ch/bio/en/groups/allard/"&gt;COMMONS Lab&lt;/a&gt;
 is dedicated to the exploration and establishment of novel knowledge management solutions (from knowledge acquisition to knowledge organization and knowledge dissemination) in the field of natural products. Here, computational metabolomics outputs and relevant metadata are transformed in and combined to 
 &lt;a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linked_data#Linked_open_data"&gt;Linked Open Data&lt;/a&gt;
 and handled via semantic web technologies. The lab is strongly committed to follow the Open Science ideals.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Renato Bruni</title><link>https://www.dbgi.org/team/bruni-renato/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.dbgi.org/team/bruni-renato/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Sergio Rasmann</title><link>https://www.dbgi.org/team/rasmann-sergio/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.dbgi.org/team/rasmann-sergio/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Stephanie Tamdem Guetchueng</title><link>https://www.dbgi.org/team/tamdem-guetchueng-stephanie/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.dbgi.org/team/tamdem-guetchueng-stephanie/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Tarcisio Mendes de Farias</title><link>https://www.dbgi.org/team/mendes-tarcisio/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.dbgi.org/team/mendes-tarcisio/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Thomas Freeth</title><link>https://www.dbgi.org/team/freeth-thomas/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.dbgi.org/team/freeth-thomas/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Tito Damiani</title><link>https://www.dbgi.org/team/tito-damiani/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.dbgi.org/team/tito-damiani/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Tom Pickering</title><link>https://www.dbgi.org/team/pickering-tom/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.dbgi.org/team/pickering-tom/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Tomáš Pluskal</title><link>https://www.dbgi.org/team/tomas-pluskal/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.dbgi.org/team/tomas-pluskal/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Vlastimil Rybka</title><link>https://www.dbgi.org/team/rybka-vlastimil/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 0